            "bodyHinglish": "Naren ke bank passbook mein ₹ 85 jama hain. Wo school canteen mein roz ₹ 6 kharch karta hai. Mummy ne shart rakhi: \"Passbook mein kam se kam ₹ 25 hamesha bache rehne chahiye.\" Naren ne socha: kitne din tak canteen ka kharcha chalega?\n\nd din baad passbook mein 85 − 6d rupaye bachenge, aur shart hai **85 − 6d ≥ 25**. Naren ne Class 9 wali equation ki aadat se kaam kiya: 85 ko doosri taraf bheja, to −6d ≥ 25 − 85, yaani **−6d ≥ −60**. Phir usne dono taraf −6 se divide kiya aur likha: **d ≥ 10**.\n\nMummy ne dekh kar kaha: \"Naren, 11 din baad dekho. 85 − 66 = 19 bachte hain, jo 25 se kam hain. Tumhara jawab kehta hai d = 11 theek hai, par shart toot gayi!\" Naren hairaan: har kadam to Class 9 jaisa tha, phir galti kahan hui?\n\nGalti ek hi jagah thi: **negative number se divide karte waqt sign ulatna padta hai.** Kyun? Aur kab ulatna hai aur kab nahi? Yahi is topic ka kaam hai."
