            "body": "Ab tak ke alag-alag sawaal ek hi chart mein rakhte hain.\n\n```\n Sawaal padho: kya diya hai, kya chahiye?\n              :\n              v\n Kahani mein \"theek itna\" (=) hai?  --haan--->  EQUATION: ek jawab\n              :\n            nahi: at most, at least, more than, fewer than\n              :\n              v\n Replacement set kya hai?\n    ginti (bus, rope, marks) ---> N, W ya Z: dots\n    naap (km, GB, taapmaan)  ---> R: shading\n              :\n              v\n Kitni hadein?\n    ek hadd            ---> ax + b < c jaisi inequation\n    ek expression par do hadein ---> double inequation (teen hisse)\n    do alag shartein   ---> \"aur\": overlap (∩),  \"ya\": milao (∪)\n              :\n              v\n Negative number se guna ya bhaag? ---> sign ulto (double mein dono)\n              :\n              v\n Hal, phir STORY CHECK. Hadd decimal aur jawab integer?\n    at most ---> neeche ka integer,  at least ---> upar ka integer\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.6** – Method chooser. Upar se neeche chalo: pehle equation ya inequation, phir replacement set, phir hadon ki ginti, phir sign ka sawaal, aur aakhir mein story check aur rounding.\n\n| Suraagh (sawaal mein kya dikha) | Kya karein | Kahan seekha |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Theek itna\", \"barabar\" | Equation, ek jawab | Topic 1, Part C |\n| at most, at least, more than, fewer than | Inequation, symbol table se ≤, ≥, >, < | Topic 1, Part A |\n| ginti (bus, rope, marks) ya naap (km, GB) | N, W, Z ke dots ya R ki shading | Topic 1, Part D; Topic 3, Part C |\n| Negative se guna ya bhaag | Sign ulto, double mein dono sign aur hadein chhote se bade | Topic 2, Part B; Topic 4, Part B |\n| Ek expression par do hadein | Double inequation, teeno hisson par ek saath kaam | Topic 4, Part A |\n| Do alag shartein, \"aur\" / \"ya\" | Overlap (∩) / milana (∪), number line par dono banao | Topic 4, Part C aur Part D |\n| End point andar hai ya bahar? | < aur > par o, ≤ aur ≥ par @ | Topic 3, Part A |\n| Hadd decimal, jawab integer | Rounding ki disha: at most neeche, at least upar | Is topic, Part A |\n| Koi jawab nahi ya har value jawab | Khaali set ya poora replacement set | Topic 4, Part C |",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab tak ke alag-alag sawaal ek hi chart mein rakhte hain.\n\n```\n Sawaal padho: kya diya hai, kya chahiye?\n              :\n              v\n Kahani mein \"theek itna\" (=) hai?  --haan--->  EQUATION: ek jawab\n              :\n            nahi: at most, at least, more than, fewer than\n              :\n              v\n Replacement set kya hai?\n    ginti (bus, rope, marks) ---> N, W ya Z: dots\n    naap (km, GB, taapmaan)  ---> R: shading\n              :\n              v\n Kitni hadein?\n    ek hadd            ---> ax + b < c jaisi inequation\n    ek expression par do hadein ---> double inequation (teen hisse)\n    do alag shartein   ---> \"aur\": overlap (∩),  \"ya\": milao (∪)\n              :\n              v\n Negative number se guna ya bhaag? ---> sign ulto (double mein dono)\n              :\n              v\n Hal, phir STORY CHECK. Hadd decimal aur jawab integer?\n    at most ---> neeche ka integer,  at least ---> upar ka integer\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.6** – Method chooser. Upar se neeche chalo: pehle equation ya inequation, phir replacement set, phir hadon ki ginti, phir sign ka sawaal, aur aakhir mein story check aur rounding.\n\n| Suraagh (sawaal mein kya dikha) | Kya karein | Kahan seekha |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Theek itna\", \"barabar\" | Equation, ek jawab | Topic 1, Part C |\n| at most, at least, more than, fewer than | Inequation, symbol table se ≤, ≥, >, < | Topic 1, Part A |\n| ginti (bus, rope, marks) ya naap (km, GB) | N, W, Z ke dots ya R ki shading | Topic 1, Part D; Topic 3, Part C |\n| Negative se guna ya bhaag | Sign ulto, double mein dono sign aur hadein chhote se bade | Topic 2, Part B; Topic 4, Part B |\n| Ek expression par do hadein | Double inequation, teeno hisson par ek saath kaam | Topic 4, Part A |\n| Do alag shartein, \"aur\" / \"ya\" | Overlap (∩) / milana (∪), number line par dono banao | Topic 4, Part C aur Part D |\n| End point andar hai ya bahar? | < aur > par o, ≤ aur ≥ par @ | Topic 3, Part A |\n| Hadd decimal, jawab integer | Rounding ki disha: at most neeche, at least upar | Is topic, Part A |\n| Koi jawab nahi ya har value jawab | Khaali set ya poora replacement set | Topic 4, Part C |"
