            "bodyHinglish": "Akhil ki Mummy ne almari ke upar se steel ki katoriyon ka ek set utaara. Teen katoriyan ek ke andar ek fit thi: sabse chhoti beech wali mein, beech wali sabse badi mein. Akhil ne ruler se unke muh (diameter) naape: **8 cm, 12 cm aur 18 cm.**\n\n\"Mummy, ye teeno sahi fit hote hain, kyunki har katori agli se ek jitni gunaa chhoti hai,\" usne kaha. Phir usne ratio nikaale: chhoti aur beech wali ka 8 : 12 = 2 : 3, aur beech wali aur badi ka 12 : 18 = 2 : 3. \"Arre, dono ratio barabar hain!\" Mummy ne hanskar poochha, \"To agar sirf sabse chhoti (8) aur sabse badi (18) katori ka naap pata ho, to beech wali ka naap tum bina naape bata sakte ho?\" Akhil ne copy mein 12 × 12 = 144 aur 8 × 18 = 144 likha. \"Ye to barabar nikle! Ittefaq hai ya rule?\"\n\nAaj hum is sawaal ka jawab denge. Aur ye bhi dekhenge: agar sirf chhoti aur beech wali pata ho to teesri kaise nikalein, aur do alag-alag ratio ko ek saath teen cheezon ke ratio mein kaise badlein."
