            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Topic 1 mein humne dekha ki do figures similar tab hote hain jab unke corresponding angles barabar hon **aur** corresponding sides ek hi ratio (scale factor k) mein hon. Ab sawaal ye hai: triangle ke andar ek chhoti si **parallel line** kheench dein, to kya hota hai? Is topic ka seedha jawab ek khoobsurat theorem hai, jo Class 9 ke Mid-point Theorem ka **bada bhai** hai: wahan line sirf beech se jaati thi, yahan line kahin se bhi jaa sakti hai, aur phir bhi sides ek hi ratio mein katti hain. Aage ke Topic 3 mein jo similarity ke tests aayenge, unki neev yahi theorem hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Topic 1 mein humne dekha ki do figures similar tab hote hain jab unke corresponding angles barabar hon **aur** corresponding sides ek hi ratio (scale factor k) mein hon. Ab sawaal ye hai: triangle ke andar ek chhoti si **parallel line** kheench dein, to kya hota hai? Is topic ka seedha jawab ek khoobsurat theorem hai, jo Class 9 ke Mid-point Theorem ka **bada bhai** hai: wahan line sirf beech se jaati thi, yahan line kahin se bhi jaa sakti hai, aur phir bhi sides ek hi ratio mein katti hain. Aage ke Topic 3 mein jo similarity ke tests aayenge, unki neev yahi theorem hai."
